{
  "_comment": [
    "Device profiles for screen-capture shot ingestion (ADR-014).",
    "A profile is the *only* device-specific thing in the pipeline: it names the tile",
    "labels to look for, which ShotData field each one feeds, and how to read the sign",
    "off the qualifier the device prints next to the number. No pixel coordinates —",
    "the parser locates cells geometrically, so a profile survives a different photo",
    "framing, screen size, or crop.",
    "Fields with target=null are boundary-only: they are not stored, but finding them",
    "keeps the neighbouring cell from spilling into their column."
  ],
  "profiles": [
    {
      "device": "hd_golf",
      "title": "SHOT DATA",
      "value_span_ratio": 3.5,
      "blank_markers": ["---", "--", "—", "- - -"],
      "fields": [
        {
          "label": "Shot Distance",
          "target": "total_distance",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "yards"
        },
        {
          "label": "Carry",
          "target": "carry_distance",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "yards"
        },
        {
          "label": "Bounce & Roll",
          "aliases": ["Bounce Roll", "Bounce and Roll"],
          "target": "bounce_and_roll",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "yards"
        },
        {
          "label": "Ball Speed",
          "target": "ball_speed",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "mph"
        },
        {
          "label": "Launch Angle",
          "target": "launch_angle",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees"
        },
        {
          "label": "Club Speed",
          "target": "club_head_speed",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "mph"
        },
        {
          "label": "Club Path",
          "target": "club_path",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["I>O", "I O", "IO", "1>0", "I>0"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["O>I", "O I", "OI", "0>1", "O>1"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Custom",
          "target": null,
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "label": "Club Face Angle",
          "target": "club_face_angle",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["OPEN"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["CLOSED", "CLOSE"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Spin",
          "target": "spin_rate",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "rpm"
        },
        {
          "label": "Smash Factor",
          "target": "smash_factor",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "ratio"
        },
        {
          "label": "Impact Position",
          "target": "impact_position",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "label": "Shot Type",
          "target": "shot_type",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "label": "Horizontal Angle",
          "target": "launch_direction",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["R", "RIGHT"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["L", "LEFT"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_comment": [
            "The one tile HD Golf prints already signed ('-9.3 °'), and its polarity is the",
            "opposite of the ShotData contract's (+ = fade). Both real shots on disk print a",
            "negative axis while the screen's own Shot Type tile beside them reads FADE, and",
            "on both the face sits >10 ° open to the path, which curves the ball right for",
            "this right-handed golfer. Three readings of one screen agreeing, so printed_sign",
            "is -1 rather than a guess. validate.py cross-checks the stored sign against Shot",
            "Type on every parse, so if this is ever wrong for some shot shape it says so",
            "instead of quietly storing a fade as a draw.",
            "sign_tokens stays: if HD Golf ever prints '9.3 ° R', the word still wins."
          ],
          "label": "Spin Axis",
          "target": "spin_axis",
          "kind": "number",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "printed_sign": -1,
          "sign_tokens": [
            { "tokens": ["R", "RIGHT"], "sign": 1 },
            { "tokens": ["L", "LEFT"], "sign": -1 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_comment": [
            "The bay layout's last tile, the vertical partner of Impact Position. In this",
            "fork only: the frozen parser's copy never gains it (M34 decision 1), and",
            "crates/screen/tests/profile_fork.rs declares it as the one difference.",
            "Its label scores 0.9375 against 'Impact Position' and the other way round,",
            "so the two are told apart by the parser's tie rule (TIE_MARGIN), never by",
            "this file. No alias: an alias would widen exactly the overlap the rule weighs."
          ],
          "label": "Impact Position V",
          "target": "impact_position_v",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": ["Full Swing's grid screen (M42). Labels carry their units; aliases without the unit cover the reads that drop it (the M42 plan's finding 2). Path and face print their own sign, a minus being left, which for a right-handed golfer is ShotData's convention, so neither has a sign rule (finding 8). Total Yd is printed twice (call 7), Apex in feet (call 8), and ball direction and sidespin are signed by a lit letter (calls 4, 5)."],
      "device": "full_swing",
      "title": "SHOT DATA",
      "value_span_ratio": 6.0,
      "split_merged_labels": true,
      "blank_markers": ["---", "--", "—", "- - -"],
      "fields": [
        { "label": "Shot Result", "target": null, "kind": "text" },
        { "label": "Total Yd", "aliases": ["Total"], "target": "total_distance", "kind": "number", "unit": "yards", "printed_twice": true },
        { "label": "To Hole Yd", "aliases": ["To Hole Ft", "To Hole"], "target": null, "kind": "text" },
        { "label": "Carry Yd", "aliases": ["Carry"], "target": "carry_distance", "kind": "number", "unit": "yards" },
        { "label": "Club Speed Mph", "aliases": ["Club Speed"], "target": "club_head_speed", "kind": "number", "unit": "mph" },
        { "label": "Ball Speed Mph", "aliases": ["Ball Speed"], "target": "ball_speed", "kind": "number", "unit": "mph" },
        { "label": "Path Deg", "aliases": ["Path"], "target": "club_path", "kind": "number", "unit": "degrees" },
        { "label": "Face Deg", "aliases": ["Face"], "target": "club_face_angle", "kind": "number", "unit": "degrees" },
        { "label": "Ball Direction Deg", "aliases": ["Ball Direction"], "target": "launch_direction", "kind": "number", "unit": "degrees",
          "lit_sign": [ { "token": "L", "sign": -1 }, { "token": "R", "sign": 1 } ] },
        { "label": "Launch Angle", "target": "launch_angle", "kind": "number", "unit": "degrees" },
        { "label": "Apex Ft", "aliases": ["Apex"], "target": "apex_height", "kind": "number", "unit": "yards", "printed_unit": "feet" },
        { "label": "Smash Factor", "target": "smash_factor", "kind": "number", "unit": "ratio" },
        { "label": "Backspin Rpm", "aliases": ["Backspin"], "target": "backspin", "kind": "number", "unit": "rpm" },
        { "label": "Sidespin Rpm", "aliases": ["Sidespin"], "target": "sidespin", "kind": "number", "unit": "rpm",
          "lit_sign": [ { "token": "D", "sign": -1 }, { "token": "F", "sign": 1 } ] }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
